Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against jin-s13/xtcocoapi]

NumPy 2 removed the deprecated NPY_OWNDATA flag alias from its Cython
declarations (numpy/__init__.pxd). Cython then resolves np.NPY_OWNDATA as a
Python attribute at run time, so every mask function that hands a C buffer
to an ndarray (decode, area, iou, toBbox) raises
AttributeError: module 'numpy' has no attribute 'NPY_OWNDATA'.
NPY_ARRAY_OWNDATA is the same flag and is declared by NumPy 1.x as well.
pycocotools carries the identical change (ppwwyyxx/cocoapi).

diff --git a/xtcocotools/_mask.pyx b/xtcocotools/_mask.pyx
index 1b55292..428e5ec 100644
